==============================================================================
1. youki (OCI container runtime) — modified, pinned, run as a separate program
==============================================================================

Upstream:  https://github.com/youki-dev/youki
Version:   0.7.0
License:   Apache License, Version 2.0

kata runs every stage inside a rootless OCI container started by youki. kata's
youki provider (`kata-provider-youki`) execs youki as a separate program; no
kata binary links it. config/youki-pin.toml pins the exact Nix store path and sha256 of the
youki binary kata will run, and `kata host setup` realises that path.

kata does not use the stock nixpkgs build. nix/youki.nix rebuilds the same
nixpkgs derivation of the same upstream release with the `seccomp` cargo
feature enabled ("systemd,seccomp"). Without that feature youki drops a
bundle's seccomp filter instead of installing it.

Modification. nix/youki-0.7.0-foreground-prereap.patch is authored by kata
and changes youki's crates/youki/src/commands/run.rs:

  It moves the foreground WNOHANG reap loop into a `reap_children` helper and
  calls it once right after the signal mask is set, so a container init that
  exits before the mask is set is reaped and does not leave `youki run`
  waiting forever.

The patch is a backport of the same fix in upstream youki commit c06504aa7e
(youki-dev/youki#3639), which had not been released when the patch was
written. One behavior differs from upstream: a signal-killed init reports the
bare signal number, as 0.7.0 does, where upstream reports 128 + signal.

Modification. nix/youki-0.7.0-atomic-state-save.patch is authored by kata
and changes youki's crates/libcontainer/src/container/state.rs:

  `State::save` writes the container's state document to a temporary file in
  the same directory, syncs it, and renames it over `state.json`, instead of
  truncating `state.json` and writing it in place, so a concurrent reader sees
  the previous document or the new one and never a truncated one.

Redistribution. The flake's `youki` package (`nix build .#youki`) is the
patched binary. `just cache-push` uploads it to kata's binary cache,
katacode.cachix.org, together with the `kata` package.

libseccomp — LGPL-2.1-only, version 2.6.1, from nixpkgs. The seccomp-enabled
youki links it dynamically (libseccomp.so.2), so it is part of youki's runtime
closure. No kata binary links it.

